# text
# c1: Kshana-Desktop-0.41.0-macos-universal.dmg.sha256
seg-8f550352f109 = The disk image is signed and notarised for macOS. Its SHA-256 checksum is published beside it on the release page as <a1><c1/></a1>; check it before you open the image. Versions for Windows and Linux are not published yet. Until they are, <s1>Kshana Studio</s1> runs the same engine in any modern browser, with nothing to install.

# text
seg-823be34f8e02 = <b>The Studio, natively.</b> Runs, charts, tables, the scenario kinds, the bundled examples and the CCSDS (Consultative Committee for Space Data Systems) and SP3 (Standard Product { "3" }) exports run on the natively linked engine: the same calls as the WebAssembly engine in the browser, so a run gives the same figures.

# text
seg-d262c212eafc = <b>Live receiver trust.</b> The trust page can score a receiver live from a serial or USB port, a TCP stream or a growing file (NMEA { "0183" }, read only, every five seconds). Advisory software, not certified navigation equipment: the operator remains responsible for navigation.

# text
seg-09b21204dc19 = <b>IQ recordings.</b> A recording view shows power, a waterfall and the spectrum at a cursor for ci8, cu8, ci16 and cf32 recordings and SigMF metadata. It has no control that writes a file or transmits.

# text
seg-954aadf09e12 = <b>Read only.</b> Kshana Desktop drives no radio hardware and transmits nothing.

# text
seg-e8844beb1351 = Licence and support

# text
seg-904aaf612999 = Kshana Desktop runs the open engine and is free to use under the AGPL-3.0 (GNU Affero General Public License, version { "3" }), like the rest of the open core. For a commercial licence, support terms or a deployment across your organisation, write to <a1>contact@ashforde.org</a1>.

